 ## Overview
-Component Ablation Diagnostics evaluates the contribution of individual components within a neural scene reconstruction pipeline by systematically removing architectural branches, loss terms, or input signals and comparing performance against a baseline [S1, S2, S3]. It is distinguished from sibling methods like [L1 Norm Regularization](7273-l1-norm-regularization-for-transfer-functions.md) and [Neural Latent Regularization](10334-neural-latent-regularization.md) by its diagnostic nature: rather than actively regularizing the model during training, it isolates marginal utility through parallel or sequential variant training [S1, S2, S3].
